      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What you're describing sounds like a deep sense of despair, which is a very heavy burden to carry. It makes perfect sense to feel that the effort didn't yield the expected return when everything you built has vanished. Instead of thinking about starting over, perhaps you could focus on finding a small, manageable piece of comfort right now, something that requires no grand plan. Remember that even when the big structure is gone, the capacity to feel and to seek support remains.",
